{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791049637,"nonce":"ThXVaGHvann86MKL/0vT93T9bOk=","title":"Embed: handler segments for a host that switches stacks on one thread","message":"A host that runs Zyntax code on several stacks of one thread (caribou's tasks) needs a with-scope left open on one stack to stay out of scope on the others, and to come back when that stack runs again. The executor already does this per task (task_handler_enter/leave/forget, docs/ASYNC_EFFECTS_FIBERS.md 5.9), but those live in a private module. Expose them on TieredRuntime with ids from HostTask's id space: new_handler_segment, enter_handler_segment(id) -\u003e HandlerSegmentScope, leave_handler_segment(id, scope), forget_handler_segment(id).","files":null}]}